---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Code from "../../../components/Code.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../../../config/site";
import { breadcrumbs, article } from "../../../data/jsonld";

const desc = "Use Showsteps from an AI agent: the showsteps command line with JSON output and exit codes, the local showsteps-mcp server, file format, and worked examples.";

const editExample = `showsteps info onboarding.showsteps --json
showsteps steps onboarding.showsteps --json          # find the step ids
showsteps edit-step onboarding.showsteps --id s4 \\
  --title "Open **Billing** in the sidebar" \\
  --description "You need the Admin role to see this." --out reviewed.showsteps
showsteps export reviewed.showsteps --format md,pdf,skill --out ./out --json`;

const stepsJson = `{
  "title": "Reset your password",
  "steps": [
    { "action": "navigate", "url": "https://app.example.com/login" },
    { "action": "click", "target": "Forgot password" },
    { "action": "type", "target": "Email", "value": "jane@example.com" },
    { "action": "type", "target": "New password", "masked": true },
    { "action": "click", "target": "Reset password" },
    { "action": "note", "title": "Check your inbox for the confirmation email." }
  ]
}`;

const newExample = `showsteps new --from-steps steps.json --out reset-password.showsteps --json
showsteps export reset-password.showsteps --format skill --out ./skill --json`;

const mcpConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "showsteps": { "command": "npx", "args": ["-y", "@showsteps/mcp"] }
  }
}`;

const path = "/docs/agents/";
---
<Base title="Showsteps for agents: CLI and MCP" description={desc} path={path}
  jsonLd={[article({ headline: "Showsteps for agents", description: desc, path, dateModified: "2026-09-28" }), breadcrumbs([{ name: "Showsteps", path: "/" }, { name: "For agents", path }])]}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">For agents</span>
      <h1>Showsteps for agents</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A person records a task in the Chrome extension. You, an agent, can read, fix, export and create guides from files, with no
        network, no account and no API key. The same text is in <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/blob/main/AGENTS.md`}>AGENTS.md</a> in the repo and in <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">What you can do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Validate and inspect a guide file.</li>
          <li>Rewrite step titles and descriptions, hide steps, regenerate titles.</li>
          <li>Export Markdown, self-contained HTML, PDF, DOCX, a Playwright script, or a replayable agent skill.</li>
          <li>Create a guide from steps you write (no screenshots needed), then hand the file to a person to open in the extension.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Everything works offline on local files. Passwords and other sensitive fields are never stored in a guide: typed values in
          those fields are masked as <code>•••</code> and no tool prints them.
        </p>

        <h2>Files</h2>
        <p>A guide is either:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>something.showsteps</code>: a zip with <code>guide.json</code> and <code>images/&lt;stepId&gt;.png</code>, or</li>
          <li>a bare <code>guide.json</code>. Screenshots are picked up from an <code>images/</code> folder next to it, if present.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Every command and tool accepts both. The schema is versioned (v1). Key fields: <code>title</code>, and <code>steps[]</code> with
          <code>id</code>, <code>action</code>, <code>target</code> (name, role, locators), <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>,
          <code>page.url</code> and <code>skipped</code>.
        </p>

        <h2>CLI</h2>
        <Code code={`npx -y @showsteps/cli --help`} caption="shell" />
        <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="CLI commands" tabindex="0">
          <table class="compare">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Command</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps validate &lt;file&gt; [--json]</code></th><td>Checks the file against the schema. Exit 1 lists every problem.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps info &lt;file&gt; [--json]</code></th><td>Title, step counts, actions, pages, sensitive steps, screenshot counts.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps steps &lt;file&gt; [--json]</code></th><td>Steps with id, title, action, target, skipped and sensitive flags.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps edit-step &lt;file&gt; --id &lt;id&gt; [--title T] [--description D] [--skip|--unskip] [--out F]</code></th><td>Edit one step. Overwrites the file unless <code>--out</code> is given.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps regen-titles &lt;file&gt; [--out F]</code></th><td>Regenerate generated titles. Hand-edited titles are kept.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps export &lt;file&gt; --format md|html|pdf|docx|playwright|skill|all --out &lt;dir&gt; [--no-images] [--credit] [--json]</code></th><td>Write exports. Comma lists work: <code>--format md,pdf</code>. Exports carry no Showsteps branding unless you pass <code>--credit</code>.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>showsteps new --from-steps &lt;steps.json&gt; --out &lt;file.showsteps&gt; [--title T]</code></th><td>Create a guide from a step list.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3>Rules you can rely on</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>--json</code> prints exactly one JSON object on stdout and nothing else. It always has <code>"ok": true|false</code>. Failures look like <code>{`{"ok": false, "error": {"code": "invalid|usage|io", "message": "...", "errors": [...]}}`}</code>.</li>
          <li>Human messages and errors go to stderr.</li>
          <li>Exit codes: <code>0</code> ok, <code>1</code> invalid input (bad guide, unknown step id, bad steps file), <code>2</code> usage error, <code>3</code> file error (missing or unwritable path).</li>
          <li>Relative paths resolve against the current directory.</li>
          <li><code>SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH</code> fixes timestamps written by <code>new</code> and by edits, for reproducible output.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Export layout</h3>
        <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Export layout" tabindex="0">
          <table class="compare">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Format</th><th scope="col">Files written to <code>--out</code></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>md</code></th><td><code>guide.md</code>, <code>images/*.png</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>html</code></th><td><code>guide.html</code> (one file, images inlined, print-ready)</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>pdf</code></th><td><code>guide.pdf</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>docx</code></th><td><code>guide.docx</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>playwright</code></th><td><code>replay.spec.ts</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>skill</code></th><td><code>skill/SKILL.md</code>, <code>skill/steps.json</code>, <code>skill/replay.spec.ts</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:1em"><code>--json</code> returns <code>{`{"ok": true, "files": ["/abs/path", ...]}`}</code>. Steps with <code>skipped: true</code> are left out of every export.</p>

        <h3>Example: fix wording, then export</h3>
        <Code code={editExample} caption="shell" />

        <h3>Example: write a guide from scratch</h3>
        <p><code>steps.json</code> can be an array, or an object with a <code>title</code> and <code>steps</code>:</p>
        <Code code={stepsJson} caption="steps.json" />
        <Code code={newExample} caption="shell" />
        <p>
          Step fields: <code>action</code> (<code>navigate</code>, <code>click</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>select</code>, <code>check</code>,
          <code>press</code>, <code>scroll</code>, <code>hover</code>, <code>note</code>), <code>title</code> (generated when omitted, required for
          <code>note</code>), <code>description</code>, <code>target</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>value</code>, <code>optionText</code>, <code>key</code>,
          <code>checked</code>, <code>masked</code>, <code>page</code> and <code>skipped</code>. Later steps inherit the last URL. Titles you give are treated as
          hand-edited and survive <code>regen-titles</code>. Every problem in the file is reported at once, so fix them in one pass.
        </p>
        <p>Guides made this way have no screenshots. Exports still work, and a person can open the file in the extension to review it.</p>

        <h2>MCP server</h2>
        <p><code>showsteps-mcp</code> speaks MCP over stdio. It needs no network and no keys. Files are passed by absolute path.</p>
        <Code code={`claude mcp add showsteps -- npx -y @showsteps/mcp`} caption="Claude Code" />
        <Code code={mcpConfig} caption="Claude Desktop (claude_desktop_config.json) and Cursor (.cursor/mcp.json)" />
        <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="MCP tools" tabindex="0">
          <table class="compare">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">Inputs</th><th scope="col">Returns</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>validate_guide</code></th><td><code>path</code></td><td><code>{`{valid, steps}`}</code> or <code>{`{valid: false, errors}`}</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>guide_info</code></th><td><code>path</code></td><td>Title, counts, actions, pages, sensitive steps</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>list_steps</code></th><td><code>path</code>, <code>include_skipped?</code></td><td>Ordered steps with ids</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>edit_step</code></th><td><code>path</code>, <code>step_id</code>, <code>title?</code>, <code>description?</code>, <code>skipped?</code>, <code>out_path?</code></td><td>Updated step and changed fields</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>regenerate_titles</code></th><td><code>path</code>, <code>out_path?</code></td><td>Number of titles changed</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>export_guide</code></th><td><code>path</code>, <code>format</code>, <code>out_dir</code>, <code>include_images?</code>, <code>credit?</code></td><td>Absolute paths written</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row"><code>create_guide_from_steps</code></th><td><code>out_path</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>steps[]</code>, <code>description?</code>, <code>start_url?</code></td><td>Path, id, step count</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:1em">
          Results are JSON in both the text content and <code>structuredContent</code>. Invalid guide content is reported as data by
          <code>validate_guide</code>. Everything else that fails (missing file, unknown step id, relative path, malformed steps) returns
          <code>isError: true</code> with an <code>error.code</code> of <code>invalid</code>, <code>usage</code> or <code>io</code> and the list of problems.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>edit_step</code> and <code>regenerate_titles</code> overwrite the file unless you pass <code>out_path</code>. Prefer
          <code>out_path</code> when a person has not asked you to change the original.
        </p>

        <h2>Working with people</h2>
        <p>
          The recording is a human&rsquo;s account of a task. A sensible split: you fix wording, structure and exports; the person reviews
          screenshots and redactions in the extension (<code>.showsteps</code> files open there directly) before sharing. Send them the file
          path, not the contents.
        </p>
        <p>See also: <a href="/record-workflow-as-agent-skill/">record a workflow as an agent skill</a> and <a href="/convert-clicks-to-playwright-test/">convert clicks to a Playwright test</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
